an losing cooperation and that joining Turkey would bring significant problems. Therefore, option A is the correct inference from the given statement. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>C<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\nThis option suggests that the EU can either get Turkey's full cooperation or avoid the troubles of Turkish membership altogether.\nThe context indicates that the EU needs Turkey for strategic reasons but also faces significant problems if Turkey joins. This suggests that the EU cannot achieve both full cooperation and avoiding all problems simultaneously.\nTherefore, option C is the correct inference from the given statement. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>A<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\nAfter re-evaluating the options, the correct inference from the given statement is that the EU cannot both obtain Turkey's full cooperation and completely avoid the difficult problems of Turkish membership. Therefore, the correct option is A. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>A<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>",
