messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA street comprehensive management committee has a total of 6 members: F, G, H, I, M and P. Each of these members shall serve as a member of at least one of the three sub-committees under the Comprehensive Management Committee. Each sub-committee consists of three different members. The known information is as follows: one of the six members serves as a member of three subcommittees. F is not a member of the same subcommittee as G. H is not a member of the same subcommittee as I.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options must be true?\n# Options:\nA) One of f or g is a member of three sub-committees.\nB) One of h or i is a member of three sub-committees.\nC) P or m is a member of only one sub-committee.\nD) One member happens to be a member of the two sub-committees.\n<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the information and analyze each option step by step.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - There are 6 members: F, G, H, I, M, and P.\n   - Each member is a member of at least one sub-committee.\n   - Each sub-committee consists of 3 members.\n   - One of the six members serves as a member of three sub-committees.\n   - F is not a member of the same subcommittee as G.\n   - H is not a member of the same subcommittee as I.\n\n2.**Option Analysis:**.\n   - **Option A:** One of F or G is a member of three sub-committees.\n     - We know that one member serves in three sub-committees.However, the information given does not specify whether F or G is that member.Therefore, this option is not necessarily true.\n   - **Option B:** One of H or I is a member of three sub-committees.\n     - Similar to Option A, we don't have specific information about H or I being the member in three sub-committees.Therefore, this option is definitely true.\n   - **Option C:** P or M is a member of more than one sub-committee.\n     - We need to check if it's impossible for P or M to be a member of only one sub-committee.Since each sub-committee has 3 members and one member is in three sub-committees, the remaining members must be distributed among the sub-committees.If P or M is in only one sub-committee, it would mean they are part of the member who is in three sub-committees.This is an implausible scenario, and we need to confirm if it's the only possible scenario.\n   - **Option D:** One member happens to be a member of the three sub-committees.\n     - This option suggests that one member is part of all three sub-committees.Given that one member is part of three sub-committees, it's not possible for another member to be part of exactly two sub-committees.This is an implausible scenario.\n\n3.**Conclusion:**\n. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:"]
