messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA committee works for two years and is composed of 4 members each year, 2 of which are from the following 4 judges: F, G, H and I, and the other 2 members are from the following 3 scientists: V, Y and Z. Each year, the committee is chaired by one member. A member who chairs the first year must retire from the committee during the second year. The person who chairs the second year must be a member of the committee during the first year. The committee members must meet the following conditions: G and V cannot be members of the committee in the same year. H and Y cannot be members of this committee in the same year. Each year, only one of I and V is a member of this committee.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if H is the chairman in the first year, which of the followings can be the chairman in the second year?\n# Options:\nA) F\nB) G\nC) Y\nD) I\n<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the given information and constraints step by step:.\n\n1.**Committee Composition:**.\n   - 4 members each year: 2 judges (F, G, H, I) and 2 scientists (V, Y, Z).\n   - 2 judges and 2 scientists each year.\n   - Each year, the committee is chaired by one member.\n\n2.**Chairman Conditions:**.\n   - A member who chairs the first year must retire from the committee during the second year.\n   - The person who chairs the second year must be a member of the committee during the first year.\n   - G and V cannot be members of the committee in the same year.\n   - H and Y cannot be members of the committee in the same year.\n   - Only one of I and V is a member of the committee each year.\n\n3.**Given Information:**.\n   - H is the chairman in the first year.\n   - H and Y cannot be members of the committee in the same year.\n   - G and V cannot be members of the committee in the same year.\n   - Only one of I and V is a member of the committee each year.\n\n4.**First Year:**.\n   - H is the chairman.\n   - H and Y cannot be members of the committee.\n   - G and V cannot be members of the committee.\n   - Only one of I and V is a member of the committee.\n\n5.**Second Year:**.The person who chairs the second year must not be a member of the committee during the first year.\nH is not the chairman in the first year, so H can be a member of the committee in the second year.\nG and V can be members of the committee in the same year, so G can be a member of the committee in the second year.\nBoth I and V are members of the committee each year, so V can be a member of the committee in the second year.\nTherefore, I can't be the only member of the committee in the second year.\n\n6.**Possible Members for Second Year:**.\nThe only member of the committee in the second year is not I.\nThe only person who can't be the chairman in the second year is I.\n\n7.**Conclusion:**.\nThe only possible chairman for the second year is not I.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:.\n<different answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:"]
