messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nPersonal company refers to a company based on the personal credit of its shareholders; joint-investment company refers to a company whose assets are formed by the respective capital contributions of the company\'s shareholders as the basis for its credit; a joint-personal joint venture is a company with both of the above properties,credit basis.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following companies is Personal company?\n# Options:\nA) The registered capital of a company is the sum of the share capital paid by all shareholders.\nB) All the shares of a company are 100% held by the independent founder of the company, and the company employs a number of experienced professional managers in charge of different businesses.\nC) A company\'s capital chain was broken due to poor management. when filing for bankruptcy, the entire registered capital was counted, and the shareholders\' personal property was not affected\nD) The assets of a company are mortgaged with all the personal property of the shareholders\n<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the definitions provided and analyze each option to determine which one fits the definition of a "Personal company.".\n\n1.**Definition Recap:**.\n   - **Personal Company:** A company based on the personal credit of its shareholders.\n   - **Joint-Investment Company:** A company whose assets are formed by the respective capital contributions of the company\'s shareholders as the basis for its credit.\n   - **Joint-Personal Joint Venture:** A company with both properties of a Personal Company and a Joint-Investment Company.\n\n2.**Option Analysis:**.\n   - **Option A:** "The registered capital of a company is the sum of the share capital paid by all shareholders.".\n     - This option describes a Joint-Investment Company, as it mentions the capital contributions of shareholders forming the company\'s assets.\n     - It does not mention the personal credit of the shareholders, so it does not fit the definition of a Personal Company.\n\n   - **Option B:** "All the shares of a company are 100% held by the independent founder of the company, and the company employs a number of experienced professional managers in charge of different businesses.".\n     - This option describes a situation where the company is owned by an independent founder, which aligns with the concept of a Personal Company, as the credit basis is the personal credit of the founder.The assets of a company are not mortgaged with any personal property of the shareholders.. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
