messages:   11%|#         | 64/600 [15:30<10:01,  1.12s/it]["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe prehistoric fish Tiktaalik is the earliest known animal with fingers. Since variations were so great among prehistoric fish species, Tiktaalik would not have stood out as unusual at the time. However, Tiktaalik' s fingers were an important development in animal evolution because it is likely that Tiktaalik is an ancestor to the many land animals with fingers.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, the statements above, if true, most strongly support which one of the following?\n# Options:\nA) Tiktaalik is not the ancestor of any currently surviving fish species.\nB) Tiktaalik's fingers were its only feature to play a significant role in the development of modern land animals.\nC) The evolutionary significance of tiktaalik could not be determined just through comparison to fish species of its time.\nD) No fish without fingers would ever be able to move on land.\n<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the context and analyze each option step by step:.\n1.The context tells us that Tiktaalik is the earliest known animal with fingers and that it would not have stood out as unusual among prehistoric fish species due to the great variations among fish species.\n2.Despite this, Tiktaalik's fingers are highlighted as an important development in animal evolution because it is likely that Tiktaalik is an ancestor to many land animals with fingers.\n3.Now, let's examine each option:.\nTiktaalik is the ancestor of all currently surviving fish species.\n      - This option aligns with the context, which suggests that Tiktaalik is likely the common ancestor to all fish species alive today. Therefore, this option is correct.\n   B) Tiktaalik's fingers were insignificant in the development of modern land animals.\n      - The context does not provide information about the significance of Tiktaalik's fingers in the evolution of land animals. This option cannot be definitively supported by the given information.. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:"]
