messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nBigamy refers to the act of having a spouse and marrying another person, or marrying someone knowing that he or she has a spouse.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is bigamy?\n# Options:\nA) Li xiaoqing has been in love with wang gang for many years, held a formal engagement ceremony, and has accepted many gifts from wang gang's family, but later li xiaoqing tore up the marriage contract and married a foreign man\nB) Huang was mistreated by his husband, so he fell in love with a colleague in her factory, and the two sometimes secretly traveled together. when his husband knew about it, he sued the court and sued huang for bigamy with his colleague. but huang said that her real husband was the colleague\nC) A's family lives in a remote village in jiangxi. he is married and has a son. during a trip, he was abducted by his fellow villager to a remote mountain village in anhui, sold to qiu in the village, and became qiu's wife without registration\nD) Sun married zhou for a year and decided to divorce because of personality differences. zhou's parents immediately took their daughter home. half a year later, without going through the divorce formalities, sun married another non-local woman, and zhou also married a man from a neighboring village\n<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze each option and determine which one fits the definition of bigamy provided in the context.Bigamy is defined as having a spouse and marrying another person, or marrying someone knowing that he or she has a spouse.Let's examine each option step by step:.\n\nLi Xiaoqing was never in love with Wang Gang, never had an engagement ceremony, and never accepted any gifts from Wang Gang's family. In fact, Li Xiaoqing never tore up a marriage contract or married a foreign man.. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:"]
