messages:   18%|#7        | 105/600 [25:36<08:53,  1.08s/it]['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nObligatory alternative action refers to a situation in which the actor has committed an illegal act and caused the result, but the result cannot be avoided even if he abides by the law.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is an optional act of obligation?\n# Options:\nA) When a was driving normally, a pedestrian named wang rushed to a from the sidewalk and wang was injured\nB) B drunk driving, pedestrian wang also drunk, from the sidewalk suddenly rushed to b, wang was injured\nC) C driving speeding, pedestrian wang across the road, c too late to brake, wang hit\nD) D overload driving, pedestrian wang across the road, fortunately, ding emergency brake, did not hit wang\n<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the definition of "obligatory alternative action" and analyze each option based on this definition..\n\n1.**Definition Recap**: Obligatory alternative action refers to a situation where the actor has committed an illegal act and caused the result, but the result cannot be avoided even if he abides by the law.This means that the illegal act was unavoidable, and the actor could not have prevented the result regardless of their compliance with the law.\n\n2.**Option Analysis**:.The driver a was driving normally, and the injury occurred because of the pedestrian\'s action. The pedestrian wang\'s action (rushing to the road) is not illegal. This scenario fits the definition of obligatory alternative action because the driver\'s legal act (driving normally) did not cause the injury.. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
