messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAn international team analyzed the genetic material decay rate of DNA extracted from an extinct MOA skeleton fossil and found that although the short DNA fragment may exist for 1 million years, the half-life of 30 or more base pair sequences under certain conditions is only about 158000 years. According to this, a scientist believes that reconstructing dinosaurs with ancient DNA is similar to the story of the film Jurassic Park is impossible to happen.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings, if true, refutes the scientist's point of view most?\n# Options:\nA) Although jurassic park is a science fiction film, it should also have factual basis\nB) The fossil samples studied above may be contaminated by human dna\nC) Environmental factors will affect the decay rate of genetic materials such as dna\nD) The sequence of base pairs of  dinornis and dinosaur is different\n. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:"]
