messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOne of the characteristics of spotted geese in flight is that they often fly in a certain formation, and the birds behind usually fly behind the side of the previous bird, so they have a common human formation. Some researchers believe that this formation can reduce air resistance and flight energy consumption, but opponents believe that if it is to reduce resistance, birds should choose a straight line formation, because one flight after another can minimize the air resistance that followers need to overcome.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if which of the following is true, which of the following options most questions the opponent\'s conclusion?\n# Options:\nA) During the flight, the leading geese will change positions with their rear companions from time to time, otherwise they will easily be exhausted.\nB) When flying, the spotted geese deviate from their companions in front of them, which can not minimize the air resistance, but can greatly reduce the physical energy consumption required for ascent.\nC) Spotted geese will have the need to determine the direction when flying, so they will not always fly in the shape of human.\nD) In speed skating competitions, athletes often advance in the shape of people. one athlete is in the front, followed by three others, and the last three players benefit from reduced resistance.\n<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step.The context provides information about the formation of spotted geese in flight and the opposing view that a straight line formation would be more efficient in reducing air resistance.The question asks which option most questions the opponent\'s conclusion that a straight line formation is more efficient.\n\nFirst, let\'s restate the opponent\'s conclusion: "If it is to reduce resistance, birds should choose a straight line formation, because one flight after another can minimize the air resistance that followers need to overcome.".\n\nNow, let\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) **During the flight, the leading geese will change positions with their rear companions from time to time, otherwise they will easily be exhausted.**.\n   - This option talks about the exhaustion of the leading geese but does not directly address the efficiency of the formation in reducing air resistance.It does not challenge the opponent\'s conclusion about the straight line formation.\n\nB) **When flying, the spotted geese deviate from their companions in front of them, which can not minimize the air resistance, but can greatly reduce the physical energy consumption required for ascent.**.\n   - This option suggests that the spotted geese deviate from their companions, which implies that the current formation (which includes deviation) does not minimize air resistance.Indirectly supports the opponent\'s conclusion that a straight line formation is more efficient in reducing air resistance.\n\nD) **In speed skating competitions, athletes often advance in the shape of people. One athlete is in the front, followed by three others, and the last three players benefit from reduced resistance.**.\n   - This option provides an example where a straight line formation leads to reduced resistance, which aligns with the opponent\'s conclusion.. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
