messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nWhy are the brain sizes of some primates larger than other animals? The reason is usually considered to be social behavior, that is, primates live in larger and more complex social groups. In order to better handle various social relationships, they Need a bigger brain.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if which of the following is true, the above point of view can\'t be questioned?\n# Options:\nA) It is easier to predict the size of the brain through the dietary characteristics of primates rather than the complexity of the community\nB) Some primates such as orangutans usually live alone, but their brains are also large\nC) The size of the cerebral cortex is not directly related to the size of the brain, but it is very important for primate cognition, spatial reasoning ability, etc\nD) Among primates, fruit-eating animals have larger brains than leaf-eating animals. this is because fruits are more dispersed in time and space, and finding fruits is a more complicated task\n<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step.The context provides a reason for why some primates have larger brains compared to other animals: it\'s due to their complex social behavior and the need to handle various social relationships.The question asks us to identify which option, if true, would make the given point of view (that social behavior is the reason for larger brain sizes in primates) unchallengeable.\n\nFirst, let\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) "It is easier to predict the size of the brain through the dietary characteristics of primates rather than the complexity of the community.".\n- This option suggests that diet is a better predictor of brain size than social complexity.If this were true, it would directly challenge the given point of view that social behavior is the primary reason for larger brain sizes in primates.Therefore, this option would make the point of view questionable, not unchallengeable.\n\nB) "Some primates such as orangutans usually live alone, but their brains are also large.".\n- This option presents a counterexample to the given point of view.It shows that some primates with large brains do not live in complex social groups.This directly challenges the idea that social behavior is the reason for larger brain sizes.Therefore, this option would make the point of view questionable, not unchallengeable.\n\nC) "The size of the cerebral cortex is not directly related to the size of the brain, but it is very important for primate cognition, spatial reasoning ability, etc.".Among primates, leaf-eating animals have larger brains than fruit-eating animals.This is because fruits are less dispersed in time and space, and finding fruits is a simpler task.. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
