messages:   25%|##4       | 148/600 [31:41<19:04,  2.53s/it]['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe literary works of the Chinese writer Mo Yan have made the hidden Chinese vernacular concerned by the readers of the world and recognized by the international literary world, which has once again proved that this judgment is that only the national is the world.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, based on this, which of the following options is correct?\n# Options:\nA) It\'s national, it\'s world\nB) If it is not national, it is not world\nC) As long as the nation is, it is the world\nD) Only the world is national\n<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and the question step by step.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - The context states that Mo Yan\'s literary works have made the hidden Chinese vernacular known to the world.\n   - It emphasizes that this recognition is due to the national aspect of his works.\n   - The statement concludes that this proves that only the national is the world.\n\n2.**Question Analysis:**.\n   - The question asks which of the given options correctly reflects the context.\n   - We need to identify the option that aligns with the statement that only the national is the world.\n\n3.**Option Analysis:**.\n   - **Option A: "It\'s national, it\'s world"**.\n     - This option suggests that if something is national, it is also world.However, the context does not support this.The context only mentions that national works are recognized by the world, not that national works are the world.\n   - **Option B: "If it is not national, it is not world"**.Based on the context, the correct option that aligns with the statement that only the national is the world is Option C: "As long as the nation is, it is the world".. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
