ing at it.\n     - This option describes a strong desire to use the Internet (watching the stock market), withdrawal reactions (feeling uneasy without looking at it), and it implies mental symptoms (feeling uneasy). However, it does not mention excessive use or any physical symptoms. Therefore, it does not fully fit the definition of Internet addiction.\n\nBased on the analysis, the option that best fits the definition of Internet addiction is Option B.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB\n</answer>",
