rgument that there is no reason to suppose that ecologically friendly detergents are less damaging.\n\nD) **Laundry detergents advertised as environmentally friendly are typically less effective than other detergents, so that larger amounts must be used.**\n   - This option suggests that ecologically friendly detergents are less effective and require more use, which could imply that they are more harmful overall. However, it does not directly address the claim about the environmental impact of the ingredients themselves. It focuses on the effectiveness and usage, which does not weaken the argument about the environmental impact of the ingredients.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, the one that most weakens the argument is option C, as it directly challenges the claim that ecologically friendly detergents are less damaging by suggesting they contain less harmful ingredients.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe correct option is C.\n</answer>",
