ct of peat harvesting on the water supply. It does not strengthen the argument about peat harvesting.\n\nAfter evaluating all the options, the one that most strengthens the argument is option B, as it provides evidence that the ecological conditions in Ireland have remained stable over centuries, implying that peat harvesting does not alter the ecological balance and thus does not threaten the water supply.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB\n</answer>",
