o not present a forbidding appearance.\nD) Although some buildings designed by famous architects are not well proportioned, all government buildings are designed by famous architects. Therefore, some government buildings are not well proportioned.\n- This option exhibits a similar flawed pattern of reasoning to the original argument. It incorrectly assumes that the property of being designed by famous architects (government buildings) is equivalent to the property of being well proportioned (some buildings designed by famous architects). This is a false equivalence, similar to the original argument's flawed reasoning.\nTherefore, the correct option is D.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
