e direct cause of the accident is the equipment failure.\n   - This statement is consistent with Statement A. If the direct cause is equipment failure, then according to Statement A, someone must have violated the operating rules. Therefore, Statement D is consistent with Statement A.\n\nGiven that only one of the statements is true, and considering the contradictions between Statements B and C with Statement A, we can conclude:\n- If Statement A is true, then Statement B and Statement C must be false.\n- If Statement D is true, then Statement A must be true, and Statement D is consistent with Statement A.\n\nTherefore, the correct option is:\nD) C is ture\n</answer>",
