ly address the relationship between tree felling and the decline of the civilization. It provides a reason for the population decline but does not provide evidence that the felling of trees was not the cause.\n\nGiven these analyses, option B is the best support for the experts' opinion because it directly challenges the commonly held belief by providing evidence that the civilization continued despite the felling of the last trees. This option directly addresses the core of the question and provides a strong counter-argument to the idea that tree felling was the primary cause of the civilization's decline.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe correct option is B.\n</answer>",
