      "text": " <think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option most weakens the argument that the city officials being prosecuted are being targeted because of their political affiliations. The argument is based on the fact that all of the officials being prosecuted were appointed by Mayor Bixby, and Mayor Stephens' predecessor and political foe, and that this suggests a political motive for the prosecutions.\nLet's analyze each option:\nA) Complaints of official corruption in city government have decreased since the anticorruption task force began operating.\n- This option does not directly address the issue of political targeting. It only mentions a decrease in complaints, which is not necessarily related to the prosecutions.\nB) Almost all of the officials who have served in city government for any length of time are appointees of mayor bixby.\n- This option weakens the argument by suggesting that it is common for city officials to be appointed by Mayor Bixby, making it less likely that the prosecutions are solely due to political affiliations. If almost all officials are appointed by Mayor Bixby, it becomes more plausible that the prosecutions are based on other factors, such as evidence of corruption.\nC) Former mayor bixby did not publicly oppose mayor stephens' establishment of the anticorruption task force.\n- This option does not directly address the issue of political targeting. It only mentions that Mayor Bixby did not oppose the task force, which is not relevant to the argument about the prosecutions.\nD) All of the members of the anticorruption task force had other jobs in city government before the task force was formed.\n- This option does not directly address the issue of political targeting. It only mentions that the task force members had other jobs, which is not relevant to the argument about the prosecutions.\nBased on the analysis, option B most weakens the argument by suggesting that it is common for city officials to be appointed by Mayor Bixby, making it less likely that the prosecutions are solely due to political affiliations.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe correct option is B.\n</answer>",
