he armadillos.\n</think>\n<answer>\nTo summarize, option B is not relevant because it discusses the survival of the tagged armadillos, which is not directly related to their territorial movement. The researcher's argument is about the distance the armadillos moved, not their survival.\n\nOption D is also not relevant because it suggests that only a few armadillos were tagged, which would make it less likely that a large majority of the recaptured armadillos were found within a few hundred yards. This would actually weaken the researcher's conclusion rather than support it. If only a few armadillos were tagged, it would be more plausible that a large majority of the recaptured armadillos were found within a few hundred yards because the researcher would have had more opportunities to tag them.\n\nTherefore, the correct assumption required by the researcher's argument is option A: \"A large majority of the recaptured armadillos did not move to a new territory in the intervening summer and then move back to the old territory by the fall.\"\n</answer>",
