ts who work outside the home have less time overall for household responsibilities, including dinner preparation. However, it does not specifically address why their dinners do not differ significantly in nutritional value, variety, or number of courses. Therefore, it does not directly resolve the discrepancy.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, the most plausible explanation for the discrepancy is provided by option B. It suggests that the difference in time spent preparing dinner is due to the fact that adults who work outside the home eat dinner at home less often, which could explain why their dinners do not differ significantly in nutritional value, variety, or number of courses.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe correct option is B.\n</answer>",
