existence of knowledgeable scholars who have no creative ability.\n\nTherefore, the correct option is:\n</think>\n<answer>\nA\n</answer><|User|>Let's try another one.\n# Context:\nThe number of students in a class is 100. 60 students are boys and 40 students are girls. 30 boys and 20 girls are in the advanced math class.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the argument supported above?\n# Options:\nA) The number of boys in the advanced math class is more than the number of girls.\nB) The number of girls in the advanced math class is more than the number of boys.\nC) The number of boys in the advanced math class is equal to the number of girls.\nD) The number of boys in the advanced math class is less than the number of girls.\nFAILED. Therefore, my final option is:\nThe correct option is:<|Assistant\uff5c> <think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's carefully analyze the given context and each option step by step.\n\n### Context Analysis:\n- Total number of students: 100\n- Number of boys: 60\n- Number of girls: 40\n- Number of boys in the advanced math class: 30\n- Number of girls in the advanced math class: 20\n\n### Question:\nWe need to determine which option best supports the given information.\n\n### Option Analysis:\n**A) The number of boys in the advanced math class is more than the number of girls.**\n- Number of boys in the advanced math class: 30\n- Number of girls in the advanced math class: 20\n- 30 > 20\n\nThis statement is true based on the given numbers.\n\n**B) The number of girls in the advanced math class is more than the number of boys.**\n- Number of boys in the advanced math class: 30\n- Number of girls in the advanced math class: 20\n- 20 < 30\n\nThis statement is false based on the given numbers.\n\n**C) The number of boys in the advanced math class is equal to the number of girls.**\n- Number of boys in the advanced math class: 30\n- Number of girls in the advanced math class: 20\n- 30 \u2260