an be true, and we need to find which one must be true, we need to check the consistency of each option:\n     - **Option A:** \"There is a pen in the second drawer.\"\n       - If A is true, then B is false. If C is true, then B is false. If D is true, then B is false. Therefore, A cannot be true if only one statement is true.\n     - **Option B:** \"There are letters in the third drawer.\"\n       - If A is true, then B is false. If C is true, then B is false. If D is true, then B is false. Therefore, B cannot be true if only one statement is true.\n     - **Option C:** \"There are books in all four drawers.\"\n       - If A is true, then B is false. If C is true, then B is false. If D is true, then B is false. Therefore, C cannot be true if only one statement is true.\n     - **Option D:** \"There are no books in the four drawers.\"\n       - If A is true, then B is false. If C is true, then B is false. If D is true, then B is false. Therefore, D must be true if only one statement is true.\n\nThus, the correct option is D.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
