population has stabilized and is showing an upward trend. It provides a direct link to the experts' belief that the policy has achieved the desired effect.\n\n**D) The government's policy to encourage childbirth is a long-term national policy.**\n- This option provides information about the duration of the policy but does not directly support the current evidence that the population is stabilizing and showing an upward trend. This option is not directly relevant to strengthening the current evidence.\n\n### Conclusion\nThe option that best strengthens the experts' belief that the policy has achieved the desired effect is the one that directly supports the current evidence of population stabilization and upward trend. Therefore, the correct option is:\n\n**C) In recent years, the total population of the country has shown a slow upward trend.**<|Assistant|> <answer>C</answer>",
