messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nXiao Li destroyed the green space beside his fence and planted cucumbers. After the community property manager found it, he reminded Xiao Li that the green space beside the guardrail is a public green space, belonging to the owner of the community. To this end, the property issued a rectification notice requiring Xiao Li to restore the green space within a time limit. Xiao Li argued: am I not from the community? Since the green space beside the fence belongs to the owner of the community, it certainly belongs to me. Therefore, I have the right to plant cucumbers on my own land.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is most similar to Xiao Wang's mistake?\n# Options:\nA) Everyone should be responsible for his wrong behavior. xiao wang is not responsible for his behavior. all xiao wang's behavior is correct\nB) All the orchids participating in the expo were ordered out. li yang bought a pot of flowers at a high price. it can be seen that li yang must buy orchids\nC) No one can read all dumas's works in one day, and no one can read the three musketeers in one day. therefore, the three musketeers is one of dumas's works\nD) The army composed of all mobi knights was invincible in europe at that time, and the king yiya was one of the mobi knights, so the king yiya was invincible in europe at that time\nFAILED. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:"]
