ists over forty have spent too long in their field.\n   - **Option D:** The first is a claim, the accuracy of which is at issue in the argument; the second is a conclusion drawn on the basis of that claim.\n     - This is correct because the first boldface is a claim (evidence) and the second boldface is the conclusion drawn from that evidence.\n\nTherefore, the correct option is: <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c> D. <think>\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
