messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe law of tea production in the world is red in the south and green in the north, that is, only high quality black tea can be produced in lower latitudes (such as India and Kenya), while high quality green tea can be produced in relatively high latitudes (25  degree~ 30  degreenorth latitude). The international price of green tea has always been higher than that of black tea. The quality of green tea in India, Indonesia and Sri Lanka, the main tea producing countries, is not high. Since the 1970s, the above three countries began to change red to green in an attempt to occupy the international green tea market, all of which ended in failure. China's famous green tea is mainly distributed in mountainous areas. with rich rural labor resources and low labor costs, the development of green tea industry has obvious comparative advantages.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following statements is consistent with the original text?\n# Options:\nA) At present, the supply of black tea exceeds the demand in the international market\nB) The price of indian green tea is higher than the international average price of green tea\nC) Chinese green tea has competitive strength in the international market\nD) There is a trend of change red to green in the international tea market\nFAILED. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:"]
