 C is the one that is most strongly contradicted by the context. The context shows that taxi drivers work fewer hours on a busy day (high income potential) compared to a slow day (low income potential), which directly contradicts the idea that people work longer when their effective hourly wage is high.\n\nTherefore, the correct option is C.\n</think>\n<answer>\nC\n</answer>",
