rmation.\nD) People who like reading are calmer than those who like watching TV: The context doesn't provide any information about the calmness of people who like reading versus those who like watching TV. This option is not supported by the given information.\n\nConsidering the analysis, the most appropriate option that captures the main point of the paragraph is B: The way of information reception affects people's behavior. This option encompasses the various ways in which reading and watching TV influence people's engagement, recall, and behavior as discussed in the context.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB\n</answer>",
