ggests that incumbents who are rightly blamed should not seek reelection, but if they do, they should not be returned. However, the context doesn't mention anything about incumbents not seeking reelection if they are rightly blamed. It only discusses the reactions based on who is blamed.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, the principle that best accounts for the contrast in reactions described in the context is option C.\n</think>\n<answer>\nC\n</answer>",
