ll conclusion is that complex passwords are necessary because they are harder to remember and thus more likely to be written down.\n   - For this conclusion to be strongly supported, we need to assume that writing down a password increases the chances of unauthorized access.\n\nTherefore, the correct assumption is provided by Option B.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB\n</answer>",
