messages:  ["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nProfessor: if both parents have type O blood, their children's blood type can only be type O. this is the law of heredity. Student: that's not true. My father has type B blood, and I have type O blood.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is most likely to be the student's understanding of the professor's statement?\n# Options:\nA) Only those with type o blood have children with type o blood.\nB) People with type o blood can't have children with type b blood.\nC) People with type b blood will always have children with type o blood.\nD) If both parents have type b blood, their children will also have type b blood.\nFAILED. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:"]
