elopment can we achieve sustainable development.\"\n   - This implies that adherence to the scientific outlook on development is a necessary condition for achieving sustainable development, but it does not guarantee it.\n   - Therefore, this option cannot be inferred from the given context.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct option that can be inferred from the given context is:\n</think>\n<answer>\nC\n</answer><|User|>Okay, let's try another one.\n# Context:\nAll students who study hard will pass the exam. Some students who study hard are also members of the debate club.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following can be inferred?\n# Options:\nA) All students who study hard are members of the debate club.\nB) Some students who study hard will not pass the exam.\nC) Some students who study hard will pass the exam.\nD) All students who study hard will be members of the debate club.\nFAILED. Therefore, my final option is:\nThe correct option is:<|Assistant\uff5c> <think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the context and analyze each option step by step.\n\n1. **Context Analysis:**\n   - The context provides two statements:\n     a. \"All students who study hard will pass the exam.\"\n     b. \"Some students who study hard are also members of the debate club.\"\n\n2. **Option A: All students who study hard are members of the debate club.**\n   - The context only states that \"Some students who study hard are also members of the debate club.\"\n   - This means that while there are some students who study hard and are members of the debate club, it does not imply that all students who study hard are members of the debate club.\n   - Therefore, this option cannot be inferred from the given context.\n\n3. **Option B: Some students who study hard will not pass the exam.**\n   - The context states that \"All students who study hard will pass the exam.\"\n   - This means that no student who studies hard will fail the exam