messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nMost plants produce chemicals that resist parasites in the process of long-term evolution. Plants commonly used by humans contain about 40 natural drugs, that is, complex chemical toxins against bacteria, fungi and other parasites. People ingest these toxins every day without poisoning, so the new harm caused by synthetic pesticides sprayed on crops is very small.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if the following statement is true, which of the followings does not undermine the above argument?\n# Options:\nA) The concentration of natural drugs in plants is much lower than that of synthetic pesticides sprayed on crops\nB) Humans have been ingesting the natural drugs contained in these plants for thousands of years and have time to adapt to them\nC) The chemical structure of synthetic pesticides is usually simpler than that of natural drugs contained in plants\nD) Natural drugs contained in plants are usually only suitable for resisting specific organisms, while synthetic pesticides are usually harmful to a variety of organisms\nFAILED. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
