      "index": 0,
      "text": " <think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the given context and analyze each option step by step.\n\n1. **Context Analysis:**\n   - The context states: \"If you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.\"\n   - This can be interpreted as a conditional statement: If P (closing all wrong doors), then Q (truth will be shut out).\n\n2. **Understanding the Conditional Statement:**\n   - The statement \"If you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out\" can be written as: \\( P \\rightarrow Q \\).\n   - This means that whenever P (closing all wrong doors) is true, Q (truth being shut out) must also be true.\n\n3. **Analyzing Each Option:**\n   - **Option A:** \"If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\"\n     - This is the contrapositive of the original statement. The contrapositive of \\( P \\rightarrow Q \\) is \\( \\neg Q \\rightarrow \\neg P \\).\n     - The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n     - Therefore, this option is correct.\n\n   - **Option B:** \"Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\"\n     - This option suggests that truth cannot be shut out unless P (closing all wrong doors) is true.\n     - This is not the same as the original statement, which only says that if P is true, Q is true.\n     - Therefore, this option is incorrect.\n\n   - **Option C:** \"If the truth is not shut out, then the door to all wrong must not be closed.\"\n     - This option suggests that if Q (truth is not shut out), then \\( \\neg P \\) (not closing all wrong doors) must be true.\n     - This is not the same as the original statement, which only says that if P is true, Q is true.\n     - Therefore, this option is incorrect.\n\n   - **Option D:** \"To accept the truth, we must reject wrong.\"\n     - This option suggests that accepting truth requires rejecting wrong.\n     - The original statement does not imply that rejecting wrong is necessary to accept truth.\n     - Therefore, this option is incorrect.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - The correct option that matches the meaning of the given statement is Option A.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA\n</answer>",
