employs eight accountants, whereas it has only two actuaries on its staff.**\n- This option highlights the relative scarcity of actuaries compared to accountants, which could make it more likely that the embezzler is an accountant. This weakens the detective's argument by suggesting that the embezzler is more likely to be an accountant.\n- **Weakened Argument**\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe option that does not weaken the detective's argument is **C**. It supports the idea that the embezzler is more likely to be an actuary due to the more closely scrutinized nature of their activities.\n\nFinal Answer: C<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c> The correct option is C. <think>\nTo summarize the reasoning process:\n1. We analyzed the detective's argument and identified the key points.\n2. We then examined each option to determine how it affects the argument.\n3. Option C is the only one that supports the detective's conclusion that the embezzler is more likely to be an actuary.\n4. The other options either weaken the argument or do not affect it in a way that supports the detective's conclusion.\n</think>\n<answer>\nC\n</answer>",
