e the price it pays for economic development. This is not necessarily true based on the context. The context does not provide a definitive link between economic development and ecological damage. While industrial pollution is mentioned as a threat to the ecological environment, it does not imply that economic development will inevitably lead to ecological damage.\nTherefore, the correct option is A.\n</answer>",
