work to symbolize nothing.**\n   - This option is about the possibility of an artwork symbolizing nothing, but it does not address the relevance of intrinsic versus extrinsic properties. It does not help in making the conclusion logically follow.\n\nD) **What an artwork symbolizes involves only extrinsic properties of that work.**\n   - This option contradicts the context. It suggests that what an artwork symbolizes involves extrinsic properties, which is contrary to the given premise that extrinsic properties are irrelevant. This option does not help in making the conclusion logically follow.\n\nAfter analyzing each option, the one that directly supports the conclusion by reinforcing the idea that only intrinsic properties are relevant is option B.\n\nTherefore, the correct option is B.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB\n</answer>",
