messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA newspaper with a very large circulation actually ceased publication. The reason is that its readers are older men with low socioeconomic status. This group of people has low spending power, so the advertising effect is very unsatisfactory, which makes advertisers lose confidence in it. Without advertisers, it can no longer run.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings can be inferred?\n# Options:\nA) Circulation is not the only condition for newspapers to strive for advertising revenue.\nB) Newspaper circulation is not attractive to advertisers.\nC) Women prefer advertising to men.\nD) Relying on advertising revenue to run a newspaper is not conducive to the development of the newspaper industry.\nFAILED. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
