messages:  ['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nMedicine believes that people who are overweight have an increased risk of high blood pressure, cardiovascular disease and type 2 diabetes, which are also risk factors for kidney disease. The researchers tested the urine of 1830 Japanese children between the ages of 6 and 14. The results showed that 27 children developed persistent proteinuria, red blood cells in the urine and other nephrotic symptoms. After comparison, it was found that the body height body mass index (B.MI) and systolic blood pressure (hypertension) of these children with abnormal urine test were significantly higher than those of children with normal urine test.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options can be seen from this passage?\n# Options:\nA) Children should pay attention to prevent the occurrence of the kidney disease.\nB) Overweight is the cause of kidney disease.\nC) More and more obese children develop kidney disease.\nD) There is a correlation between childhood obesity and the risk of kidney disease.\nFAILED. Therefore, my final option is: \nThe correct option is:']
