t alternative insecticides for resistant bollworms.\n\nD) **Whether plantings of bioengineered cotton are frequently damaged by insect pests other than bollworms**:\n   - This option would be useful because it would help us understand if the increased damage to the bioengineered cotton is due to bollworms or other pests. If other pests are frequently causing damage, it would weaken the argument that the increased damage is specifically due to corn-bred bollworms.\n\nGiven this analysis, the option that would be most useful in evaluating the argument is D. It would help us determine if the increased damage is due to bollworms or other pests, thereby supporting or refuting the argument that corn-bred bollworms are the primary cause of the increased damage.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe correct option is D.\n</answer>",
